    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, Tests run: 1, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented soft (\"possible\") duplicate detection for `POST /api/owners`. A new owner that isn't a hard identity duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone is still created, and its response now reports `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id (otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`, `possibleDuplicateOf: null`).\n\nChanges made, following the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in AGENTS.md:\n\n- **New pipeline step** `FlagPossibleDuplicate.java` \u2014 reads the built `@Val Owner`, scans `OwnerRepository.findAll()` for a same-lastName (normalized) + same-postcode + different-telephone owner, and sets the flags (lowest matching id when several match; a missing postcode never matches).\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `flagPossibleDuplicate` in after `ensureUniqueIdentity` (which still rejects hard duplicates with 409) and before `save`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the flags persist.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer) columns with accessors.\n- **schema.sql** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two `readOnly` response fields to the `Owner` schema (regenerates the DTO).\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 ignored the two new targets on the request\u2192entity mapping; the entity\u2192DTO mapping picks them up automatically by name.\n\nNote: the escalation path is unchanged \u2014 this is a soft flag on a successfully created owner (201), not an error, so no new handler was needed.",
